 "notes": [
  "Shaun set OD 4.2 m, a door that swings in and up to the roof, and the widest door (2026-11-05). Everything else is a first-order proposal by Claude.",
  "Tracked one-piece leaf, curved (Shaun). It moves in 0.11 m, lifts 0.12 m on the vertical track run, then the top rollers round a 0.12 m bend while the bottom rollers climb, and it parks convex side up under the crown. No hinge: door.motion.hingeLine is null.",
  "In-move is 0.11 m, not 0.05 m: the leaf bulges 0.1 m toward the frame, and the bulge must clear the frame top member as the leaf rises.",
  "Leaf poses: place the leaf mesh from its own frame (u along the chord from the bottom edge, w toward the convex face) at each pose using bottomRollerYZ, chordDirYZ and outerNormalYZ. outlineYZ is a coarse outline for checks.",
  "All coordinate pairs ending YZ are [y, z]. Points ending XYZ are [x, y, z].",
  "The door opens only with the bay at vacuum, so no shirtsleeve crew stand under the parked leaf.",
  "Vehicle stop moved to the new nose stop by the box rule (1.14 m). The real SLED75 top is 1.14 m (mast v7 rear goalpost); with it the nose stop could be 0.69 m. CAD tyre OD is 0.521 m; the scene vehicle still uses 0.57 m.",
  "Vehicle mast position and body width are drawing values, not CAD. Wheels, footprint, heights, loader and tiller reach are from SpaceDIRT files.",
  "Radiators, about 25 m2, stow outside on the crown and deploy. They are not placed here.",
  "Equipment boxes are layout allowances. The centre of mass in the results file uses these positions.",
  "The bridge lip lies flush with the deck when down, about 40 mm thick. The ramp head hinges at the frame front face.",
  "Ramp stowage (coordinator proposal, animation plan positions): the tracks stow in channels under a fixed grated deck plate, y 1.85 to 1.99, and rise through an S-guide at z 0.45 to 1.24. A rigid 4.8 m track cannot do this: with its head at the guide top it would rise 0.28 m at z 1.24 against 0.04 m of room. Each track is therefore 9 hinged segments of 0.53 m that lock straight as they leave the guide (proposal by Claude).",
  "The compressor box top was lowered to y 1.80 so the ramp channels clear every plenum box by 0.05 m. The deck plate and channel floors are grated or perforated so the downdraft still reaches the hopper.",
  "This file is final for the curved, tracked end door (2026-11-05). The side-door variant was stopped and has no geometry file."
 ]
}